WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.516
Five levels of arithmetic, all of it one spread

2
00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:07.208
divided by another. Now the gauge says pass, and

3
00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:10.748
nothing else. There is no reading to subtract.

4
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:15.643
But the three questions do not go away. Does one appraiser agree with

5
00:00:15.743 --> 00:00:20.553
himself. Do two agree with each other. Does either of them agree with

6
00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:25.037
the truth. Only now the answers have to be built out of counts.

7
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:29.571
So hire an appraiser who does not look at

8
00:00:29.671 --> 00:00:32.527
the parts at all. He passes every one.

9
00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:37.667
Against himself he is perfect - he never contradicts himself, because

10
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:42.668
he never decides anything. Against a colleague with the same habit,

11
00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:47.371
also perfect. And against the truth he scores ninety nine point

12
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:51.476
nine percent, because that is how many parts were good.

13
00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:56.399
And he missed one hundred percent of the bad parts. Percent agreement

14
00:00:56.499 --> 00:01:01.475
cannot see him. Nothing about the gauge, and nothing about him, entered

15
00:01:01.575 --> 00:01:04.906
that number - only the base rate of the process.

16
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.872
The fix is old and well known. Subtract the agreement two

17
00:01:10.972 --> 00:01:15.117
people would reach by chance, and report only what is left

18
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:19.582
over. That is Cohen's kappa, and it sees straight through the

19
00:01:19.682 --> 00:01:23.827
appraiser who never looks - it cannot even be computed for

20
00:01:23.927 --> 00:01:27.268
him, because chance explains everything he did.

21
00:01:27.366 --> 00:01:30.296
Now hold the percent agreement still.

22
00:01:30.396 --> 00:01:33.818
Ninety percent, every table, no exceptions.

23
00:01:33.916 --> 00:01:37.877
And move only one thing: how lopsided the stream is. As

24
00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:42.455
the agreement piles into the pass cell, kappa falls from point

25
00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:47.550
eight to point one. Same percent agreement throughout. The trouble is

26
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:51.021
which end a good process lives at - it lives at

27
00:01:51.121 --> 00:01:55.968
the right-hand end, so being capable depresses kappa all by itself.

28
00:01:57.866 --> 00:02:01.680
Which raises the question of where kappa comes from at

29
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.086
all. And the answer is the whole of this level.

30
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:09.311
Behind every go/no-go gauge there is a real dimension and

31
00:02:09.411 --> 00:02:13.391
a real instrument. The appraiser has no number, but the

32
00:02:13.491 --> 00:02:16.581
thing in his hand does, and it is the gauge

33
00:02:16.681 --> 00:02:20.587
Levels two to five built. So sweep that gauge's sigma.

34
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:25.317
Every number an attribute study reports moves, and all of them

35
00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:30.052
move together, because all of them are functions of one sigma.

36
00:02:30.152 --> 00:02:35.092
Agreement stays high and comfortable. Kappa falls off a cliff. The

37
00:02:35.192 --> 00:02:38.223
miss rate climbs. Nobody chose any of it.

38
00:02:38.316 --> 00:02:42.079
And here is where our own gauge sits. Ninety nine and

39
00:02:42.179 --> 00:02:46.670
a half percent agreement, which reads like a pass. Kappa nought

40
00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:52.427
point three four, which every published guideline calls unacceptable. Those are

41
00:02:52.527 --> 00:02:56.144
the same gauge, on the same day, measured two ways.

42
00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:03.190
Which tells you where the disagreements have to be. A part far inside

43
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.825
the limit is never failed. A part far outside is never passed.

44
00:03:07.916 --> 00:03:11.704
Here is where the parts are, and here are the limits.

45
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.124
And here is where the disagreements are - a spike at each limit,

46
00:03:16.224 --> 00:03:21.102
and nothing anywhere else. Widen the gauge and the spikes widen with it.

47
00:03:21.202 --> 00:03:25.596
The band belongs to the instrument, not to the person holding it.

48
00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:30.071
Bring it back to our own gauge, and look at the size of it.

49
00:03:30.616 --> 00:03:35.314
Six percent of everything this plant makes sits in that band, and

50
00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:40.702
it produces ninety nine percent of every disagreement the study will ever

51
00:03:40.802 --> 00:03:45.204
record. Which is why retraining the appraiser does so little.

52
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.480
One more bill to pay. A count carries less information

53
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.560
than a measurement, and the arithmetic charges for it.

54
00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:01.975
Level two settled a whole variance with ninety readings. Bounding a five

55
00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:06.797
percent miss rate to plus or minus two points needs four hundred

56
00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:11.243
and fifty seven known-bad parts - and a plant that can find

57
00:04:11.343 --> 00:04:15.990
four hundred and fifty seven bad parts has a different problem.

58
00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:20.690
Which is why the most common result of an attribute study - no

59
00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.549
escapes found - says so much less than it sounds. Zero misses in

60
00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:30.863
fifty bad parts is still consistent with a miss rate near six percent.

61
00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.743
So six levels have now described one measurement system, from a single

62
00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:42.195
reading to a gauge with no reading at all. Level seven hands

63
00:04:42.295 --> 00:04:45.534
it back to the process it was built to watch.

